{"title":"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem B","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> be TNYWR.<br />\nDetermine the positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0d7ddc03ecdef065ba09ff6b2cbcf2b85425fa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2:m:t = m:32:x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"163\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/c/46c52dfd05dd7b0fb4953b01212a31b697cce856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{m} = \\frac{m}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/2/1d21687e5c797dc5e53459a73e0d5c22cf2ba8a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\times m = 2 \\times 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec521675786f58bea29de5a6d80c98262b9d6f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{2} = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d8688331d0168cc9e96694f3d8a924fa4b18a2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\sqrt{64} = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"21\" /> (since we have positive numbers)\n</p><p>We can realize that we needed to multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c95a340af391872726bf67446774e9face7c2f04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{2} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" /> to get to the new ratio. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13bb0ad866cf4252d73f1b11ba29b17fc7124c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 4t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_A\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem A\">seat A</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5bc2ef78516fb01003693c823d005e12e9c756f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/7/267eff476e84f55b7295d31f4f272ada77cd0aa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 4 \\times 5 = \\boxed{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"131\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC\">2014 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_A\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem A\">Relay 1 Problem A</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_C&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem C (page does not exist)\">Relay 1 Problem C</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 1\">Individual 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_2\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 2\">Individual 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_3\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 3\">Individual 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 4\">Individual 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Individual 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Individual 6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_P